To determine if the string `t2 t0 t4 t2` can be generated by the given Chomsky Normal Form (CNF) grammar, we will use the CYK algorithm.

The string is `s = t2 t0 t4 t2`.
The length of the string is n = 4.

We construct a table P[i][j] where P[i][j] is the set of non-terminals that can generate the substring from index i to j (inclusive).

**Step 1: Initialize P[i][1] for substrings of length 1 (i.e., individual terminals).**

First, list all terminal productions:
't0': {NT68, NT3, NT98, NT78, NT39, NT86, NT43, NT84, NT1, NT62}
't1': {NT63, NT47, NT98, NT33, NT54, NT4, NT48, NT81, NT77}
't2': {NT97, NT84, NT1, NT77, NT7, NT68, NT52, NT53, NT80, NT5}
't3': {NT68, NT35, NT12, NT26, NT77, NT80, NT74, NT96, NT54}
